--- !u!114 &1217614279
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 1217614278}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: f4688fdb7df04437aeb418b961361dc5, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  m_Material: {fileID: 0}
  m_Color: {r: 1, g: 1, b: 1, a: 1}
  m_RaycastTarget: 1
  m_RaycastPadding: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0, w: 0}
  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: "\nFlight Control Interface Specifications: Spatial Gesture Commands\n\nThis
    document establishes the standardized operational procedures for the high-priority
    spatial gesture uplink system controlling the unmanned aerial vehicle (UAV).
    All pilots must adhere strictly to these physical hand orientations to ensure
    deterministic flight performance.\n\n1. Launch & Recovery System Configuration
    (Left Hand)\n\n\u2022 Operational Execution:\n\t\u2022 Takeoff Protocol: Extend
    the index finger and pinky finger simultaneously while keeping the middle and
    ring fingers closed (the \"Sign of the Horns\" / Rock and Roll gesture). This
    initiates the automatic arming sequence and commands an ultra-smooth vertical
    climb to a stabilized altitude.\n\t\u2022 Precision Landing: Transition the left
    hand into a fully closed fist. This overrides current flight routines to initiate
    a soft, managed vertical descent to touchdown.\n\n2. Directional Flight Steering
    & Vector Tracking (Right Hand)\n\n\u2022 Physical Hand Layout: Extend either
    the index and middle fingers together OR the index finger alone. All remaining
    digits must be fully closed into the palm. Position the palm face-down, parallel
    to the ground (analogous to placing your hand on a steering wheel).\n\u2022 Operational
    Execution:\n\t\u2022 Pitch Forward: Push the hand forward along the longitudinal
    axis to command the aircraft to accelerate forward along your hand's alignment
    path.\n\t\u2022 Lateral Roll: Translate the hand sideways along the lateral axis
    to command the aircraft to drift left or right in tandem with your movement.\n\t\u2022
    Retract/Pitch Backward: Draw the hand backward toward the operator's chest to
    command the aircraft to reverse direction and retreat toward the pilot.\n\n3.
    Dynamic Braking & Immediate Halt (Right Hand)\n\n\u2022 Physical Hand Layout:
    Transition the right steering hand immediately into a fully closed fist (all
    digits retracted into the palm).\n\u2022 Operational Execution:\n\t\u2022 Active
    Stop: Intercepting this gesture neutralizes all active horizontal velocity inputs
    instantly, initiating programmatic aerodynamic braking to bring the aircraft
    to an immediate, stable hover.\n\n4. Strategic Recall & Aerodynamic Position
    Lock (Left Hand)\n\n\u2022 Physical Hand Layout: Utilize the left hand with fully
    extended digits to issue systemic overrides.\n\u2022 Operational Execution:\n\t\u2022
    Recall to Base (Return-to-Pilot): Extend all fingers fully in an upright position
    (resembling a standard \"stop sign\") with the hand positioned away from the
    face. This commands the aircraft to initiate autonomous recall routines and return
    directly to the pilot's coordinates.\n\t\u2022 Flight Loiter Freeze: Extend all
    fingers fully with the palm facing directly toward the sky. This overrides active
    avionics subsystems to lock the aircraft into a rigid GPS Loiter position hold."
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: aa38ca27b05415d4192c5f7c52e4bad8, type: 2}
